{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#317","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#317","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#317\",\"parent_revision\":\"a2554a9dc3eceb74bab48f81a608bc1f7b2a645faba8e7ca3e99f1e7ee2fcfa6\",\"root_revision\":\"a2554a9dc3eceb74bab48f81a608bc1f7b2a645faba8e7ca3e99f1e7ee2fcfa6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe @logging agent exists (.claude/agents/logging.md) and knows how to read transcripts and produce structured work logs (Completed/Decisions/Discovered/Next Steps). But there is no automation to invoke it at the right moments. Three pieces needed: (1) A pre-compact hook that fires the logging agent to snapshot current work into a structured log file before context is lost during compression. (2) A committed log file convention (e.g., .claude/sessions/{date}-{slug}.md) so logs survive across sessions and compressions. (3) A session-start hook that reads the most recent log file and injects it as context so the new session knows what happened. The @logging agent becomes the producer, and the /session-historian skill becomes the consumer that can also search historical logs. Related: backlog item #109 (SAM Audit Trail / Observability) covers broader telemetry \u2014 this item is specifically about the agent-facing work log continuity problem.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Structured session work logs with pre-compact and session-start hooks\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Wire the existing @logging agent into pre-compact and session-start hooks to produce and consume persistent work logs, closing the context continuity gap.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. @logging agent location | AVAILABLE | .claude/agents/logging.md \u2014 produces Completed/Decisions/Discovered/Next Steps logs from transcripts\\n2. Hook event types available | AVAILABLE | PreCompact, SessionStart hooks supported by Claude Code; .claude/hooks/ directory\\n3. Log file storage convention | AVAILABLE | .claude/sessions/{date}-{slug}.md convention defined in description\\n4. Session-start context injection mechanism | AVAILABLE | SessionStart hook can write to stdout to inject context into session\\n5. Pre-compact hook can spawn @logging agent | DERIVABLE | mechanism: hook invokes agent via claude -p or spawns logging script; exact invocation needs confirmation\\n6. Log file discovery (most recent) | DERIVABLE | find .claude/sessions/ sort by date, read latest file\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all three pieces have known entry points; pre-compact agent spawn mechanism is the main design decision.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] A pre-compact hook fires the `@logging` agent to write a structured log to `.claude/sessions/{date}-{slug}.md` before context is compressed\\n- [ ] Log files survive session end; `.claude/sessions/` directory accumulates one file per session (or per compaction event)\\n- [ ] Each log file contains sections: Completed, Decisions, Discovered, Next Steps\\n- [ ] A session-start hook reads the most recent `.claude/sessions/*.md` file and injects its content as context at session startup\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files .claude/hooks/` passes on any modified hook scripts\\n- [ ] Manual test: start a session, do work, trigger compaction, verify `.claude/sessions/` contains a new log file; start a new session, verify the log content is injected as context\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/logging.md` \u2014 @logging agent (producer, read-only for this item)\\n- `.claude/hooks/` \u2014 new pre-compact hook script (JavaScript .cjs)\\n- `.claude/hooks/` \u2014 new or modified session-start hook script (JavaScript .cjs)\\n- `.claude/sessions/` \u2014 new directory for session log files\\n- `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 register new hooks (PreCompact, SessionStart events)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **developer starting a new Claude Code session**, I want **a structured work log from the previous session injected at startup** so that **I don't lose context on what was completed, decided, and discovered when the previous session ended or was compacted**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **structured session work logs with pre-compact and session-start hooks** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 identified gap in state tracking across compressions and sessions\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c8b3a0a1bcd046e10fa60fee2e4671ebe20c3726c907717b9a83f1543789776d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTBzvg\"}"}